{{also|dominó|dominò|Domino}}
==English==
{{wikipedia|Dominoes}}
[[Image:Domino (PSF).png|thumb|Two domino blocks]]

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*dem-}}
1801, borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|domino}} (1771), originally the term for a hooded garment, itself from {{der|en|ML.|domino}}, oblique case of {{m|la|dominus||lord, master}}; compare {{cog|ML.|dominicale||a kind of veil}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|dŏ'mĭnō|a=RP}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈdɒmɪnəʊ/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-domino.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{enPR|dämĭnō|a=US}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈdɑmɪnoʊ/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Wodencafe-domino.wav|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|dominoes}}

# {{lb|en|dominoes}} A [[tile]] divided into two [[square]]s, each having 0 to 6 (or sometimes more) [[dot]]s or pips (as in [[dice]]), used in the [[game]] of [[dominoes]]. {{defdate|from c. 1800}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=2000|artist={{w|A Perfect Circle|A Perfect Circle}}|title={{w|The Hollow (song)|The Hollow}}|passage='''Dominoes''' of indiscretions down<br/>Falling all around, in cycles, in circles<br/>Constantly consuming<br/>Conquer and devour}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2012-07-11|author=Tony Plakas|title=Mitt's Mormon marriage march|journal=w:Sun-Sentinel|url=https://www.sun-sentinel.com/news/fl-xpm-2012-07-11-sfl-tpcol-mitt-711-story.html|passage=The Mormon church's past anti-gay positions and its role in financing Proposition 8 – California's 2008 ban on same-sex marriage – may have been the first '''dominoes''' to fall around the faithful, but vetting Mitt Romney as a presidential candidate links the straightforward similarities between Mormonophobia and homophobia.}}
# {{lb|en|politics}} A [[country]] that is expected to [[react]] to [[event]]s in a [[neighboring]] country, according to the [[domino effect]].
# A [[masquerade]] [[costume]] consisting of a [[hooded]] [[robe]] and a [[mask]] covering the upper part of the [[face]].
#: {{syn|en|domino costume}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1749|author=Henry Fielding|title=Tom Jones|page=485|publisher=Folio Society|year_published=1973
|passage=all the women were desirous of having the bundle immediately opened; which operation was at length performed by little Betsy, with the consent of Mr Jones: and the contents were found to be a '''domino''', a mask, and a masquerade ticket.}}
#* {{RQ:Landon Ethel Churchill|page=175|volume=III|passage=The chair being announced, she fastened on her mask, and drew her '''domino''' round her, it not being her intention to display her splendid and fantastic costume till supper, when all the guests were expected to unmask.}}
#* {{RQ:Orczy Miss Elliott|chapter=The Affair at the Novelty Theatre|passage=For this scene, a large number of supers are engaged, and in order to further swell the crowd, practically all the available stage hands have to ‘walk on’ dressed in various coloured '''dominoes''', and all wearing masks.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1983|author=w:Lawrence Durrell|title=Sebastian|publisher=Faber & Faber|year_published=2004|series=Avignon Quintet|page=1007
|passage=Then he hunted for the black carnival '''domino''', supposing that it was the appropriate thing for a penitent to wear.}}
# The mask itself.
#: {{syn|en|domino mask|half mask|eyemask}}
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=1872
|year_published='''2009'''
|edition=HTML
|editor=
|author=James De Mille
|title=The Cryptogram
|chapter=
|url=http://www.gutenberg.org/dirs/2/8/4/3/28435/28435-h/28435-h.htm
|genre=
|publisher=The Gutenberg Project
|isbn=
|page=
|passage=He wore a '''domino''', but beneath it could be seen his whiskers, cut after the English fashion, and long and pendent.
}}
# The person wearing the costume.
# {{lb|en|geometry}} A [[polyomino]] made up of two squares.
#: {{syn|en|2-omino}}
# {{lb|en|music|colloquial}} A [[mistake]] in [[perform]]ing.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1932|title=The Musical Times and Singing-class Circular|page=263
|passage=Any player is liable to make a ''''domino'''' — that is to say, he goes wool-gathering and continues to play when everyone else has stopped. If he does so at a grown-up concert the fault is irredeemable {{...}}}}

